Feature: Games in the fast arena
  The [[fast arena]] plays a game of [[tag]] with no window and no [[SITL]]. Four planes play.
  The candidate is the first plane, and the three [[computer pilot]]s are the others. The
  computer pilots fly with their own hands, not with the executor. Thus they are the same for
  every candidate.

  The candidate flies the T1-S Ranger, as the computer pilots do. Its [[ground control agent]]
  gives a plan once a second, and the [[executor]] flies it 50 times a second. A small model of
  the roll and pitch controllers of ArduPilot flies the demand. The other planes reach the
  executor as tracks, late and with some lost, as from a radio.

  A plane tags another when it comes within 8 m: a virtual touch. In the simulator the touch is
  1.5 m, but the executor keeps 4 m from other aircraft, so it could never tag. Each game has a
  seed. The seed sets the wind, who is it first, the delay and the loss
  of the tracks. The same seed gives the same game.

  The score of a game is the reward of the plan for tag: -1 for each 120 s as [[it]], +0.2 for
  each tag, -0.2 for each time tagged, -0.3 for each exit from the arena and -1 for a crash. The
  plane that is it for the least time gets +1, then +0.3, -0.3 and -1.

  Expectation: A game in the arena is a game of tag with the computer pilots
    When the arena plays a game with the default executor
    Then the length of the game is 120 s
    And the players in the game are 4
    And the time the candidate flew by plan is above 90 s
    And the crashes of the candidate are 0

  Expectation: The same seed plays the same game
    The league compares two executors on the same seeds. Thus a difference in the score comes
    from the executors, not from the luck of the game.

    When the arena plays the same seed twice
    Then the two games are the same

  Expectation: The arena plays much faster than real time
    The arena plays many games at the same time, one on each core.

    When the arena plays 64 games with the default executor
    Then the speed of the arena is at least 200 times real time
